  "en": {
    "about": "English. Stop words mirror the Russian list role for role: articles, auxiliaries, prepositions and the map's own boilerplate ('what you see'). Negations are deliberately NOT stop words here: a cue phrase that says 'without' must not be covered by a comment that says the opposite. Suffixes are plural and past-tense endings only — verb '-ing' stacks with '-s' ('ceiling' vs 'ceilings') and costs more matches than it buys. Column words come from the column headers themselves plus forms that do not flip under negation; the management company adds its own in the map.",
